export anchor NightSailingStyle:
    number: 419
    screen: TravelPlanner
    name: Night sailing
    idea: The trip on a marine chart plotter run in red night mode, one hue only, a ruled data bar, a chart with crosshair waypoints and a dashed planned route, a waypoint table and physical softkeys on the case, with states told by filled or hollow shapes.
    base: dark
    palette:
        cockpit: #0a0303, the page and the style sheet
        case: #1a1312, the plotter housing and softkeys
        screen: #120505, the display ground and the sea
        land: #240a08, land on the chart and the title bar
        line: #5a1f1a, every rule and cell divider
        red: #ff5c4d, the route, waypoint numbers, headings, Not booked and the primary button
        ink: #ffc9c0, text, waypoint crosshairs, Booked and focus
        muted: #d98477, labels, captions and Flight rows
        onRed: #1a0000, text on the red button
    type:
        One monospace stack, ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Consolas,
        Liberation Mono. Base 14px at 1.45, mostly caps. Readouts 20px bold
        tabular, the title 20px bold tracked 0.14em, chart labels 15px bold,
        headings 12px bold tracked 0.14em in red, labels 11px tracked 0.12em
        in muted.
    layout:
        A dark cockpit with a faint red glow at the top. The plotter case is
        a 22px rounded charcoal housing. Inside it the screen sits on the
        left and a column of four softkeys on the right. The screen opens
        with a title bar, a lit red dot with BRIGHTWORK TRIPS NIGHT, JAPAN
        IN APRIL centred and ROUTE PLAN 01 on the right. A data bar of four
        ruled cells follows, Dates 01 to 14 APR 2027, Crew M OKAFOR plus 1,
        Fund 3,200 of 5,000 euro with a small red bar and 64 percent, and WX
        Tokyo 17 degrees HI with blossom likely. The main area splits. The
        chart on the left shows dark land and sea, depth contours, a grid, a
        north arrow, and waypoints 02 Tokyo, 04 Kyoto and 05 Osaka as
        crosshair circles on a solid red route with a dashed inner line and
        a rail label. A caption line gives the weather in full. On the right
        a Waypoints table lists WPT, Date, Leg with detail under it, and
        State. Unbooked rows carry a faint red tint. A ruled row of four pre
        departure checks closes the screen. Softkeys read BOOK TRAIN 03,
        FIND STAY 05, VIEW CHECKS and VIEW ROUTE, the first ringed in red.
        Below 980px the table drops under the chart and below 700px the
        softkeys become a row of four.
    spacing: 4px steps. 8 to 12px cell padding, 14px between screen and keys and 18px case padding.
    density: High. A four cell data bar, a chart, a six row table and four checks on one screen.
    corners: Square inside the screen. A 22px case and 10px softkeys outside it.
    borders: 1px dark red rules split every cell, and a 2px black edge round the screen.
    shadows: A deep inset vignette inside the screen, softkeys on a 3px black ledge.
    icons:
        Nautical shapes in one colour. Booked is a filled diamond, Not
        booked a dashed hollow diamond and Flight an arrowhead. Done is a
        filled square and To do a hollow square. Waypoints are crosshair
        circles.
    focus: A 3px pale red outline offset 2px.
    tone: Instrument caps and short forms such as WPT, CREW, FUND and PRE DEPARTURE CHECKS.
